# Copy to `.env` to override the defaults locally. Every variable here is
# read by Vite at BUILD time and baked into the output.
#
# THIS MATTERS FOR DOCKER: the app is built with @sveltejs/adapter-static, so
# what ships is plain HTML, CSS, and JS with no server process behind it.
# There is nothing running at request time that could read an environment
# variable, which means:
#
#   docker build --build-arg VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://example.com .   <- works
#   docker run  -e VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://example.com  image        <- does nothing
#
# In a Dockerfile that looks like:
#
#   ARG VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://indienodes.us
#   ENV VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=$VITE_SITE_ORIGIN
#   RUN npm run build
#
# Changing the origin therefore requires a rebuild, not a restart. If the
# origin ever needs to change without one, the value would have to move out
# of the bundle and into something fetched at runtime, which is a different
# design and not what this is.

# The deployed origin. Used for the absolute Open Graph / Twitter Card URLs
# and, most importantly, by the embeddable widget: it runs on other people's
# sites and so must fetch ring.json with an absolute URL.
# Default: https://indienodes.us
VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://indienodes.us

# Where the submission form on /join posts. Deliberately named for the shape
# rather than the vendor: the contract is "POST JSON, read JSON back", and the
# client neither knows nor cares what is on the other end (an n8n workflow, as
# of this writing).
#
# Leave it unset and the behaviour differs by build, on purpose:
#   npm run dev    -> the form runs against a mock backend, no n8n needed
#   npm run build  -> the form reports that submissions are closed
# The second is the important one. A production build with no backend must not
# look like it is accepting submissions it is quietly dropping.
#
# This URL is PUBLIC. It is compiled into the client bundle, because a static
# site has no server to proxy through. It is not a secret, should not be stored
# as one, and every abuse control (rate limiting, honeypot checks, duplicate
# detection) has to live on the receiving end.
# Default: unset
# VITE_SUBMISSION_WEBHOOK_URL=https://n8n.example.com/webhook/indienodes-submit

# Where the change-request form on /update posts. Deliberately the SAME
# variable as VITE_SUBMISSION_WEBHOOK_URL above, not a separate one: a
# change request needs the exact token-issue/re-verify contract issue_token
# and verify already implement, so it extends that webhook with two more
# `action` values (request_update_token, submit_update) rather than
# standing up a second workflow that would have to reimplement the same
# verification mechanism.

# Where the contact form on /contact posts. A SEPARATE variable from
# VITE_SUBMISSION_WEBHOOK_URL above — Contact is a stateless
# fire-and-forget message with no token/verify contract at all, and keeping
# it on its own webhook means it can be paused or rotated independently of
# the review pipeline. Same rules as VITE_SUBMISSION_WEBHOOK_URL: public,
# unset means dev mocks / prod says the form is closed, no secret-header
# variable exists here either (there is nowhere in this repo to hold one —
# see the note at the top of this file).
# Default: unset
# VITE_CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://n8n.example.com/webhook/indienodes-contact

# Cloudflare Turnstile (CAPTCHA), rendered on /update and /contact. Only the
# site key belongs here: this is a static site with no server of its own
# (see the note at the top of this file), so there is nowhere in this repo
# that could hold the matching secret key and actually call Cloudflare's
# siteverify API. Verification has to happen the same place submission
# validation already does — the external n8n workflow(s) the two webhooks
# above point at — which is where TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY belongs, not here.
# See docs/n8n-workflow-runbook.md for where it's configured.
#
# Create a free Turnstile site at https://dash.cloudflare.com -> Turnstile.
# Leave unset to skip rendering the widget entirely, or use Cloudflare's
# test site key (always passes, no real site needed): 1x00000000000000000000AA
# Default: unset
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Points the app at a different ring.json without touching code. Used by
# `npm run dev:fixture` to exercise the 50-entry fixture in testing/.
# Accepts `/ring.json`, a full `http://host:port/path`, or the port-only
# `:4174/ring.test.json` form (resolved against whatever host the page is on,
# so exposing the dev server to a phone needs no reconfiguration).
# Default: /ring.json
# VITE_RING_URL=:4174/ring.test.json
